    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d581">

                <pb facs="d580-2" n="2" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v03mSupp/d580-2"/>

                <head>581. Telegram 1799 from Geneva<anchor n="1" xml:id="d581-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Geneva</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1956-04-19">April 19, 1956, 6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d581-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d581-1"/>
                <p>1799. From Johnson.</p>
                <p>Comments todays meeting.</p>
                <p>Wang’s reactions to our second revision draft about as expected and probably will
                    forecast line he will take at next meeting.</p>
                <p>If at next meeting he flatly rejects our revision would propose, in addition
                    repeating as necessary arguments already made, stress his responsibility offer
                    alternative language which would meet our minimum criteria of: (a) obviating
                    possibility distortion declaration into renunciation by United States its
                    position re self-defense and (b) make explicit renunciation of force applicable
                    Taiwan area as well as elsewhere.</p>
                <p>Would appreciate Department’s comments.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Gowen</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
